# Build output, and the corpora and crash artifacts a local run accumulates.
target
corpus
artifacts
coverage

# `seeds/` is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds the committed, read-only seed
# inputs every target starts from — the cron merges them into its corpus and
# the coverage workflow replays them, so a cold or evicted corpus cache still
# has something to run. They were unreachable while this file ignored them:
# the workflows read `seeds/<target>` but nothing could ever be committed
# there, so coverage reported "No corpus or seed inputs found" and exited
# green. `check_targets.sh` now fails when a target has none.

# Tracked, overriding the repo-root rule: this workspace is not covered by the
# root lockfile, so without one here every CI run re-resolves from scratch and
# is at the mercy of upstream yanks.
!Cargo.lock
